{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2238","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2238","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2238\",\"parent_revision\":\"9063d57998ab989bfac56cb608c72bee9038684b025019c1d90758da5ef4007b\",\"root_revision\":\"9063d57998ab989bfac56cb608c72bee9038684b025019c1d90758da5ef4007b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"swarm-patterns Pattern 3 (Self-Organizing) requires the orchestrator to write per-task `TaskCreate` calls before spawning workers\\\"\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: .claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md lines 109-114\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-10\\n  - Content: |\\n      TaskCreate({\\n        subject: \\\"Review auth.rb\\\",\\n        description: \\\"Review auth.rb for security and code quality issues\\\",\\n        activeForm: \\\"Reviewing auth.rb...\\\"\\n      })\\n      // ... repeat for each file\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Pattern 3 code example shows TaskCreate being called once per file with the comment indicating manual repetition for each file in the pool.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"Lines 109-114 of swarm-patterns/SKILL.md show the orchestrator must manually call `TaskCreate` once per file\\\"\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: .claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md lines 109-114\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-10\\n  - Content: Direct TaskCreate call with \\\"// ... repeat for each file\\\" comment confirms orchestrator manually calls once per file\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The code pattern and explicit repeat comment verify the claim exactly as stated.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"There is no mechanism to read a markdown file containing checkbox items (`- [ ]`) and auto-generate `TaskCreate` calls\\\"\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: Codebase grep for checkbox+TaskCreate, marko usage in plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-10\\n  - Content: |\\n      Found marko usage only for parsing backlog item bodies (backlog_core/parsing.py, run_backlog_server.py).\\n      Found no skill, script, or mechanism that:\\n      - Reads markdown files with checkbox items\\n      - Parses them as task definitions\\n      - Auto-generates TaskCreate calls\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Extensive codebase search found marko used for backlog parsing but no dedicated mechanism for checkbox-to-TaskCreate conversion.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"The dispatch skill operates on already-decomposed SAM task YAMLs, not on free-form markdown checkbox lists\\\"\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md lines 18-21, 43\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-10\\n  - Content: |\\n      Q -->|\\\"Yes \u2014 SAM plan exists\\\"| SAM[\\\"SAM Dispatch<br>Minimal prompt \u2014 task file has everything\\\"]\\n      ...\\n      SAM dispatch (task file is the delegation)\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Dispatch documentation explicitly requires pre-existing SAM task files and does not support free-form markdown input.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"marko AST walking is the mandated markdown parser per `.claude/CLAUDE.md` markdown-AST policy\\\"\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: .claude/CLAUDE.md line 523\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-10\\n  - Content: |\\n      Markdown AST Parsing: Use `marko` for any task that requires parsing markdown structure\\n      (headers, list items, inline code, bold, tables, section extraction). Do NOT write regex\\n      parsers for markdown.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Policy explicitly mandates marko for markdown structure parsing and prohibits regex-based approaches.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"Octogent's 'Todo-Driven Delegation' pattern is cited at `./research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md`\\\"\\nVERDICT: REFUTED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: Directory listing of /home/user/claude_skills/research/agent-frameworks/\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-05-10\\n  - Content: |\\n      Files present: AutoResearchClaw.md, Trellis.md, agentscope.md, agno.md, ai-agents-frameworks.md,\\n      arxitect.md, bmad-method.md, browser-harness-js.md, claude-code-harness.md, composure.md,\\n      copilotkit.md, cursor-cookbook.md, dify.md, esp-claw.md, everything-claude-code.md,\\n      get-shit-done.md, gitagent.md, google-adk.md, gstack.md, json-render.md, liteagents.md,\\n      micro-agent.md, mission-control.md, orchestra.md, pi-mono.md, ra-aid.md, ruflo.md,\\n      solace-agent-mesh.md, superpowers.md, tersa.md\\n      \\n      NO FILE NAMED: octogent.md\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The claimed file does not exist in the agent-frameworks research directory. The citation cannot be verified.\\n\\n---\\n\\nSUMMARY:\\n- Claims 1-5: VERIFIED against source code and documentation\\n- Claim 6: REFUTED \u2014 file does not exist\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Assessment: Markdown checkbox file to swarm task pool helper for self-organizing dispatch\\nDate: 2026-05-11\\nGoal: Build /swarm-from-markdown skill that reads a markdown file, parses unchecked - [ ] items via marko AST, and emits TaskCreate calls + spawns workers.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. swarm-patterns SKILL.md Pattern 3 gap identified at lines 109-114 | Status: AVAILABLE (verified by Read)\\n2. marko AST parsing mandated in .claude/CLAUDE.md | Status: AVAILABLE (verified by Read)\\n3. Skill directory must be one level under .claude/skills/ | Status: AVAILABLE (verified by CLAUDE.md subdirectory rules)\\n4. No existing swarm-from-markdown skill directory | Status: AVAILABLE (verified by directory listing)\\n5. scripts/ directory exists for reference script | Status: AVAILABLE (verified by directory listing)\\n6. octogent.md present at research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md | Status: AVAILABLE (verified by ls after rebase onto cd641a0 \u2014 file added in that commit)\\n7. Todo-Driven Delegation pattern documented in octogent.md lines 51-53 | Status: AVAILABLE (verified by Read)\\n8. Citation URL for octogent: https://github.com/hesamsheikh/octogent | Status: AVAILABLE (from octogent.md resource_url field)\\n9. Acceptance criteria measurable signals from discovery artifact | Status: AVAILABLE (5-item fixture, skill dir path, script path, SKILL.md worked example all concrete)\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 9\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nVERDICT: APPROVED \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE. Groomer may proceed.\\n\\nResolution notes (2026-05-11):\\n- Conditions 6+7+8 unblocked: octogent.md was added to main in commit cd641a0; file confirmed present at research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md after rebase.\\n- Condition 9 unblocked: adopting discovery artifact measurable signals as ACs (auto-mode resolution).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/swarm-from-markdown/SKILL.md` \u2014 New file. Defines the `/swarm-from-markdown` skill invocation contract, `marko` AST walking workflow, `TaskCreate` emit pattern, and self-organizing worker prompt template. This is the authoritative specification of the new interface. No existing producer is modified. | Risk: LOW | Why: Purely additive; no existing consumers need migration.\\n\\n- `scripts/markdown_to_task_pool.py` \u2014 New file. Reference implementation that parses unchecked `- [ ]` items via `marko` and emits `TaskCreate` call sequences. Implements the contract defined in the skill. Subject to full CI quality gates (ruff, ty, markdownlint on `.md` files). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: New Python script in `scripts/` must satisfy all ruff/ty rules; `marko>=2.2.2` is already a root dependency so no dependency change needed, but the script must use PEP 723 inline metadata or be called via `uv run`. Coverage gate (`**/scripts`) applies automatically.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\nNone identified. This is a new capability. No existing code calls `swarm-from-markdown` or `markdown_to_task_pool`. Verified via grep across all `.py`, `.md`, `.yaml`, and `.json` files.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml` \u2014 `marko>=2.2.2` is already declared as both a root dependency and a dev dependency. No changes needed. `tool.coverage.run.source = [\\\"**/scripts\\\"]` means the new script is in coverage scope automatically. `pytest.ini_options.pythonpath` does not include root `scripts/` \u2014 if pytest tests for the new script are added under `tests/`, they will be discovered; tests placed directly in `scripts/` would not be discovered unless named `test_*.py` and the root `scripts/` path is added to `pythonpath`. | Risk: LOW | Why: No change required to existing config; coverage is automatic; test placement must follow existing conventions.\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml::tool.ty.environment.extra-paths` \u2014 Root `scripts/` is not listed (only specific sub-paths like plugin scripts are listed). The new `scripts/markdown_to_task_pool.py` will still be type-checked via `include = [\\\"**/*.py\\\"]` in `tool.ty.src`, but if it imports from shared modules those must be resolvable. If the script is self-contained (PEP 723 inline deps) there is no impact. | Risk: LOW | Why: `marko` is a root workspace dep and will resolve. Self-contained scripts are the established pattern.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` \u2014 Pattern 3 (Self-Organizing) and Workflow 3 (lines 99-151, 413-460) show the manual `TaskCreate` loop with comment `// ... repeat for each file`. After this item ships, the pattern still works but has a better automation path that is not referenced. The \\\"Related Skills\\\" section at line 576-582 lists only `swarm-primitives`, `swarm-spawning`, `swarm-operations`. The new `swarm-from-markdown` skill is a natural addition to that list and to Workflow 3's task-pool creation step. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Documentation is not wrong but becomes incomplete \u2014 Pattern 3 / Workflow 3 callers will not discover the new automation unless `swarm-patterns` is updated to reference it.\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/orchestrating-swarms/SKILL.md` \u2014 This facade skill currently lists exactly 4 specialist skills (`swarm-primitives`, `swarm-spawning`, `swarm-operations`, `swarm-patterns`). The Quick Start flowchart routes \\\"Build a workflow from a recipe\\\" to `swarm-patterns`. A user building a self-organizing swarm from a markdown file would not discover `/swarm-from-markdown` via the facade. | Risk: LOW | Why: The facade works correctly without the reference, but discoverability of the new skill is reduced. The omission does not cause incorrect behavior, only incomplete guidance.\\n\\n- `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` \u2014 The backlog item cites this as the source pattern (\\\"Todo-Driven Delegation\\\"). The file does NOT exist (verified via file existence check and grep \u2014 Fact-Check in the item: REFUTED). The SKILL.md must NOT cite `./research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` as its source, or it will contain a broken internal link. If the implementer creates `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` as part of this item, the citation would then be valid; otherwise the claim must use an external URL or be dropped. | Risk: HIGH | Why: SKILL.md citation policy (`CLAUDE.md` Citation Requirements section) requires cited sources. A broken internal link in the new SKILL.md violates the citation requirement and produces a dead reference that misleads future agents.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 The `lint-python` job runs `prek run ruff --all-files` and `prek run ruff-format --all-files`. The `typecheck-ty` job runs `ty check .` which includes `**/*.py` per `pyproject.toml`. The `lint-markdown` job runs `markdownlint-cli2 --all-files`. All three jobs will automatically check the new files. No CI config changes are needed. | Risk: LOW | Why: Additive files automatically enter all existing quality gates. The new Python script must pass ruff (all rules including ANN, D, DOC, etc.) and ty type checking; the new SKILL.md must pass markdownlint.\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml::tool.ruff.src` \u2014 Includes `\\\"**/scripts\\\"` in `src` array. The new `scripts/markdown_to_task_pool.py` falls within scope. Ruff will apply all configured rules including `ANN` (type annotations required), `D` (docstrings required), `from __future__ import annotations` isort rule. The script must satisfy these out of the box. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Other scripts in `scripts/` lack per-file exceptions in `tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores` for root `scripts/`. Full rule set applies. ANN and D violations will fail CI.\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 Hooks run on all files. The new SKILL.md and Python script will be caught by all applicable hooks on first commit. No config change needed. | Risk: LOW | Why: Standard behavior; no special hook configuration required.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` \u2014 Instructs AI orchestrators to manually write `TaskCreate` calls per item in the task pool (Pattern 3, Workflow 3). After this item ships, this instruction becomes incomplete \u2014 the AI is not told to consider `/swarm-from-markdown` when the source is a markdown checkbox file. The instruction is not wrong, but it misses the automation shortcut. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: AI following `swarm-patterns` will continue to write TaskCreate calls manually even when a markdown file is the source. The new skill goes undiscovered without a cross-reference in the agent instruction.\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-insight-extractor.md` \u2014 References `swarm-patterns` skill (confirmed via grep). Read to confirm whether the reference is to Pattern 3 specifically. If it references the swarm task-pool pattern, it may benefit from knowing about the new markdown helper. No code change is triggered, but discoverability is affected. | Risk: LOW | Why: The agent's primary function (insight extraction) is not related to task-pool creation from markdown files; cross-reference relevance is low.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| Path | Role | Connection | Action | Risk |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `.claude/skills/swarm-from-markdown/SKILL.md` | producer | New file; defines the skill interface | CODE_CHANGE (create) | LOW |\\n| `scripts/markdown_to_task_pool.py` | producer | New file; reference implementation | CODE_CHANGE (create) | MEDIUM |\\n| `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` | agent-instruction | Pattern 3 / Workflow 3 document the manual step this item automates; Related Skills section needs cross-reference | CONTENT_UPDATE | MEDIUM |\\n| `.claude/skills/orchestrating-swarms/SKILL.md` | agent-instruction | Facade listing specialist skills; new skill not yet listed | CONTENT_UPDATE | LOW |\\n| `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` | documentation | Claimed citation source \u2014 file does not exist; new SKILL.md must not cite a non-existent path | CONTENT_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `pyproject.toml` | configuration | `marko` already declared; coverage and ruff scopes apply automatically; pythonpath for tests | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` | ci | Ruff, ty, markdownlint automatically gate new files | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `.pre-commit-config.yaml` | ci | All hooks apply to new files on first commit | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: LOW-MEDIUM\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` (does not exist) \u2014 if the new SKILL.md cites this path as source, it creates a broken citation that violates the Citation Requirements policy and misleads future agents. The implementer must either create the research entry or cite an external URL.\\n  - `scripts/markdown_to_task_pool.py` \u2014 the new Python script enters the full ruff/ty quality gate with no per-file exceptions. ANN, D, DOC, and all other active rules apply. A script that fails any of these will block CI.\\n  - `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` \u2014 Pattern 3 / Workflow 3 become incomplete without a cross-reference to `/swarm-from-markdown`; AI orchestrators following this skill will miss the automation.\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - documentation (broken citation for non-existent octogent.md research entry)\\n  - verification (new Python script must satisfy full CI quality gate with no relaxations)\\n  - documentation (swarm-patterns discoverability gap for the new automation path)\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - The non-existence of `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` (cited in the item as the source pattern) is a scope expansion: either the research entry must be created as part of this item, or the citation must be replaced. This was flagged as REFUTED in the item's Fact-Check section.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface (N/A \u2014 no existing consumers)\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated (swarm-patterns Related Skills + Workflow 3 task-pool comment; orchestrating-swarms facade)\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated (swarm-patterns Pattern 3 / Workflow 3 cross-reference)\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (N/A \u2014 additive change only)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated (verify new Python script passes ruff + ty; SKILL.md passes markdownlint)\\n- [ ] Broken citation resolved (create research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md OR replace citation with external URL before shipping SKILL.md)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED** with one content validation concern\\n\\n### Rationale\\n\\nThe proposed `swarm-from-markdown` skill extends the established swarm orchestration pattern library in a direction consistent with the product mission and historical design.\\n\\n**Mission Consistency**: The Claude Skills repository provides modular skills for Claude Code. The development-harness plugin explicitly owns \\\"process orchestration (stage sequencing, gating, looping)\\\" (CLAUDE.md line 190), and swarm-patterns documents \\\"recipes and patterns for Claude Code multi-agent workflows\\\" (swarm-patterns/SKILL.md frontmatter). This proposed feature fills a documented gap in Pattern 3 (Self-Organizing) \u2014 currently orchestrators manually write TaskCreate calls for each markdown checkbox item (swarm-patterns/SKILL.md lines 109-114). Automating this workflow step is a natural extension of the existing pattern library.\\n\\n**Design Principle Alignment**:\\n- **Markdown AST Parsing**: The item correctly specifies `marko` for checkbox parsing, consistent with `.claude/CLAUDE.md` line 523 which mandates marko for markdown structure parsing and prohibits regex-based approaches. \u2713\\n- **Skill Directory Structure**: The proposed location `.claude/skills/swarm-from-markdown/SKILL.md` follows the one-level-deep convention documented in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 422-429. \u2713\\n- **Citation Requirements**: The item acknowledges Octogent's \\\"Todo-Driven Delegation\\\" as the source pattern (Acceptance Criteria section). However, the Fact-Check section definitively establishes that `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` does not exist. Per `.claude/CLAUDE.md` Citation Requirements (lines 437-462), \\\"every factual claim in skill documentation requires a cited source.\\\" The new SKILL.md must not reference a non-existent internal path \u2014 either the research entry must be created during implementation, or the citation must use an external URL or be omitted.\\n\\n**Historical Direction**: Review of commit history shows minimal recent changes to swarm-patterns/SKILL.md (only one commit touching it: 7a7ca83), indicating stability of the pattern library. The proposed addition is purely additive with no modifications to existing Pattern 1-2 or removal of manual TaskCreate workflows. The design extends, not reverses, the established pattern taxonomy.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| violates-design-principle | SKILL.md citing `./research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` as source pattern when file does not exist | Citation Requirements: \\\"Every factual claim in skill documentation requires a cited source\\\" | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 437-462; Fact-Check section of #2238 (REFUTED) |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n1 concern identified: **violates-design-principle** regarding the citation requirement. The content validation issue is resolvable during implementation by either creating the research entry or replacing the citation with an external URL or omitting it. The feature itself (markdown checkbox parsing via marko AST, TaskCreate emission, self-organizing swarm spawning) is aligned with product mission and design principles.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **markdown checkbox file to swarm task pool helper for self-organizing dispatch** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md \u2014 pattern: Todo-Driven Delegation (todo.md as execution surface for worker generation)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:c55d900661a7d83b3593f56b6a6dd4ad -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-10)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nThis is a new capability \u2014 there is no failure to reproduce. The observable gap is:\\n\\n1. Open `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` and navigate to Pattern 3 (Self-Organizing), lines 109-114.\\n2. Observe the `TaskCreate({ subject: \\\"...\\\", description: \\\"...\\\", activeForm: \\\"...\\\" })` call followed by the comment `// ... repeat for each file`.\\n3. Search the codebase for any script or skill that reads a markdown file with `- [ ]` checkbox items and auto-generates `TaskCreate` calls: none exists.\\n4. Invoke `/swarm-from-markdown` in a Claude Code session: the skill does not exist \u2014 the command is unrecognised.\\n\\nThe absence of the automation is the observable state.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 P1 (Should-Have).\\n\\nPattern 3 (Self-Organizing) is an active and documented swarm pattern used by orchestrators building parallel task pools. The manual `TaskCreate` loop is the bottleneck any time the task source is a markdown checklist \u2014 a common artifact in this codebase (research files, todo lists, milestone plans). Automating that step reduces orchestrator boilerplate, removes the error-prone \\\"repeat for each file\\\" manual expansion, and makes the self-organizing swarm pattern accessible without hand-crafting call sequences. The feature is bounded, additive, and unblocked (RT-ICA APPROVED, 9/9 AVAILABLE). No prerequisite work is outstanding.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: No backlog item is currently blocked by this one.\\n- Bottleneck: Every orchestrator that wants to seed a self-organizing swarm from a markdown checklist must manually write one `TaskCreate` call per item. For a file with 10 items, that is 10 manual calls. For research files with 20\u201330 checkboxes, the orchestrator prompt becomes unwieldy and error-prone.\\n- Scope: The gap in `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` Pattern 3 / Workflow 3 is explicitly documented (lines 109-114 comment: `// ... repeat for each file`) but has no automation path. The `/swarm-from-markdown` skill fills that documented gap.\\n- Secondary: After delivery, `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` (Related Skills section, Workflow 3 task-pool step) and `.claude/skills/orchestrating-swarms/SKILL.md` (facade listing) will need cross-reference updates \u2014 otherwise AI orchestrators following those skills will not discover the new automation shortcut.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates the manual `TaskCreate` loop when seeding a self-organizing swarm from a markdown checklist \u2014 the most common task source in this codebase.\\n- Makes Pattern 3 (Self-Organizing) accessible with a single invocation: `/swarm-from-markdown <path> [--workers N]` instead of N hand-written `TaskCreate` calls.\\n- Checked items (`- [x]`, `- [X]`) are skipped automatically \u2014 partially-complete task lists produce only the remaining work, enabling incremental re-runs on in-progress files.\\n- Establishes `marko` AST parsing as the canonical approach for checkbox-to-task conversion, consistent with the mandated markdown policy and usable as a reference pattern for future markdown-driven automation.\\n- Adds a concrete worked example to the swarm skill library, lowering the barrier for new orchestrators who want to use the self-organizing pattern.\\n- Provides a citable source pattern (Octogent Todo-Driven Delegation, `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md`) that grounds the design in observed real-world practice.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an orchestrator invokes `/swarm-from-markdown <path-to-markdown> [--workers N]`:\\n\\n1. All unchecked `- [ ]` items in the markdown file are identified. Checked items (`- [x]`, `- [X]`) are ignored.\\n2. One `TaskCreate` call is produced for each unchecked item. The item text becomes the task subject and description. Worker IDs are assigned as `worker-0`, `worker-1`, ... based on item index (0-based).\\n3. N workers are spawned using a parameterized self-organizing prompt template. When `--workers N` is omitted, a sensible default (e.g., number of unchecked items) is used.\\n4. The resulting `TaskList()` and team name are returned to the orchestrator.\\n5. The skill cites `research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` (Todo-Driven Delegation pattern) as its source, with a worked example in SKILL.md showing sample input markdown and the resulting `TaskCreate` call sequence.\\n\\nRunning `scripts/markdown_to_task_pool.py` on a fixture markdown file with 5 unchecked items (and optionally some checked items) produces exactly 5 `TaskCreate` invocations \u2014 no more, no less.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `.claude/skills/swarm-from-markdown/SKILL.md` exists at one level deep under `.claude/skills/`\\n- [ ] `scripts/markdown_to_task_pool.py` exists and, when run on a fixture markdown file with 5 unchecked items, produces exactly 5 `TaskCreate` invocations\\n- [ ] Unchecked items (`- [ ]`) are processed; checked items (`- [x]`, `- [X]`) are skipped\\n- [ ] `SKILL.md` cites `./research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md` Todo-Driven Delegation pattern as its source\\n- [ ] `SKILL.md` includes a worked example showing input markdown and the resulting `TaskCreate` calls\\n- [ ] Optional `--workers N` flag accepted\\n- [ ] Worker IDs derive from item index: `worker-0`, `worker-1`, ...\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /swarm-patterns \u2014 Pattern 3 (Self-Organizing), Workflow 3; the documented gap this item fills |\\n| Skill | /swarm-primitives \u2014 TaskCreate, TaskList, TeamCreate API reference |\\n| Skill | /swarm-spawning \u2014 Agent spawning, worker prompt template patterns |\\n| Skill | /orchestrating-swarms \u2014 facade; will need cross-reference update after delivery |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:skill-creator \u2014 required for creating or modifying SKILL.md files |\\n| Prior work | `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` lines 109-114, 413-460 (Pattern 3 / Workflow 3 manual TaskCreate loop) |\\n| Prior 